\caption[VGIA comparisons across datasets]{Attack performance of VGIA, CAH, and CTP  when the target client trains a three-layer fully connected neural network, using full-batch FedSGD, on a local dataset of $B=2048$ samples from ACS Income (top) or CIFAR10 (bottom). (a,b,d,e) Number of correct samples and reconstruction error under varying attack-round budgets. (c,f) Number of rounds required for the adversary to identify all samples (i.e., achieve verifiability) across target datasets with different values of $\varepsilon_{\mathbf w}$. CTP$_{=}$ assumes  knowledge of $\varepsilon_{\mathbf w}$. 
%(the minimum absolute distance between the projections of any two samples along direction $\mathbf{w}$). 
